st names to their float values.\n    \n    Args:\n        p: Path to the markdown file to parse.\n        \n    Returns:\n        A dictionary where keys are test names (from TESTS list) and values are \n        the parsed float measurements.\n    \"\"\"\n    out = {}\n    for line in p.read_text().splitlines():\n        c = [x.strip() for x in line.strip(\"|\").split(\"|\")]\n        if len(c) > 2 and c[-2] in TESTS:\n            m = re.match(r\"([\\d.]+)\", c[-1])\n            if m: out[c[-2]] = float(m.group(1))\n    return out\n\ndef table(d: str, base: str):\n    \"\"\"Generate and print a summary table for a specific directory.\n    \n    Aggregates results from all markdown files in the specified directory,\n    computes means per arm and test, and prints a markdown table showing\n    performance deltas relative to the baseline arm.\n"}